The user answered "Yes, add a generic core hook" to the renderer-hook question. The follow-up task framed this as one agent-neutral renderer-selection or message-interception hook in Code Puppy core. Tern-specific rendering would then live in a Code Puppy Python plugin under `trebol/tern-plugins/code-puppy/python-plugin/`. The intended constraints are:
- fall back to Rich when no handler is registered or a handler errors;
- do not bypass authorization;
- do not install plugins silently;
- preserve the earlier uncommitted direct-TSP Code Puppy edits.

This supersedes the earlier plugin-only, no-core-change limit. It is a decision; the hook and plugin are not shown to be implemented.
